# The quality gate (`make done`): lint, format, types, tests, coverage, parallel runner.
# Re-lock: pip-compile -c requirements.txt --output-file=requirements-dev.txt requirements-dev.in
#
# THE `-c requirements.txt` IS LOAD-BEARING. setup-dev-env.sh installs both lockfiles in ONE pip
# command, so a transitive dependency they SHARE must resolve to the same version in both or pip
# refuses the whole install with ResolutionImpossible and a fresh container cannot be provisioned.
# Measured 2026-08-30: the two files were compiled independently and drifted to numpy 2.5.1 (via
# shapely, runtime) against numpy 2.5.2 (via types-shapely, dev). Constraining the dev compile to
# the runtime lock is what stops the drift recurring on the next shared dep.
ruff
pyrefly      # THE type checker (feature 142) - Rust, one-shot, no daemon
pytest
pytest-cov
pytest-xdist
pytest-testmon
types-shapely
playwright    # the browser test of the interactive map page (feature 134); `python3 -m playwright install --with-deps chromium` fetches the browser
pip-tools    # re-locks these files
